{
  "_comment": "Monster types. hp/dmg are base values multiplied by the level's hpPct/dmgPct (curves.json) / 100. expPct = the type's Exp% (average 90). radius = body radius in tiles (default 0.42, a man about as wide as his sprite), scaled by the rank sizeMult: it is the hitbox for arrows and blows and the collision body, so long four-legged beasts get more (wolf 0.45, boar 0.5). collides = false only for monsters that pass through bodies (none in Act 1); it must be written explicitly. projectile = the type shoots instead of hitting in melee: it fires at range in a straight line toward where you were (it never steers); speed in tiles/s; magic shots are not stopped by the guard unless Bulwark is up. leader = the type never spawns alone nor in champion/unique packs: a normal pack becomes '1 leader + followers' with packChance (same pack size, so Act 1 XP does not change), at most maxPerArea per area/floor; while it lives, monsters within aura.radiusTiles (not itself) get aura.stats. uniqueNames = parts combined into unique monster names: '<prefix><suffix> <epithet>'. resist = share of an element's spell damage the type ignores (negative = it takes more): the dead burn easily, casters shrug off some fire. projectile.element = the shot is all of that element: the player's resistance takes its share and armor does nothing (necromancer cold, shaman lightning). bosses: abilities are telegraphed attacks (the area shows on the ground for windupSeconds, then hits whoever is still in it: a cone of arcDegrees toward the player or a circle) or a summon; below phaseTwoAtPct of its life the boss enters phase 2 (phaseTwoStats, and the abilities of phase 2).",
